**Frames** are HTML documents embedded within other HTML documents. Each frame is a separate browsing context with its own DOM.

**Why Switching is Necessary:**

WebDriver operates in a single context at a time. By default, it's in the main page context. Elements inside frames are in a different context and cannot be accessed directly.

```java
// ❌ This won't work - element is in a frame
WebElement button = driver.findElement(By.id("buttonInFrame")); 
// NoSuchElementException!

// ✅ Must switch to frame first
driver.switchTo().frame("frameName");
WebElement button = driver.findElement(By.id("buttonInFrame")); 
// Now it works!
```

**Frame Types:**

**1. Frame (deprecated)**
```html
<frameset>
    <frame src="page.html" name="myFrame">
</frameset>
```

**2. IFrame (modern standard)**
```html
<iframe id="myFrame" src="page.html"></iframe>
```

**Three Ways to Switch to Frame:**

**1. By Name or ID:**
```java
driver.switchTo().frame("frameName");
driver.switchTo().frame("frameId");
```

**2. By Index (0-based):**
```java
driver.switchTo().frame(0); // First frame
driver.switchTo().frame(1); // Second frame
```

**3. By WebElement (most flexible):**
```java
WebElement frameElement = driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("iframe.my-frame"));
driver.switchTo().frame(frameElement);
```

**Navigation Methods:**

```java
// Switch back to main page
driver.switchTo().defaultContent();

// Switch to parent frame (from nested frame)
driver.switchTo().parentFrame();
```

**Complete Example:**
```java
public class FrameHandling {
    public void handleFrame(WebDriver driver) {
        // Main page context
        System.out.println("Main page title: " + driver.getTitle());

        // Switch to frame
        driver.switchTo().frame("contentFrame");

        // Now can interact with frame elements
        WebElement button = driver.findElement(By.id("frameButton"));
        button.click();

        // Switch back to main page
        driver.switchTo().defaultContent();

        // Back in main page context
        WebElement mainButton = driver.findElement(By.id("mainButton"));
        mainButton.click();
    }
}
```

**Key Concept:** Think of frames as separate windows within the main window. You must explicitly switch context to interact with them.

