back:
**Nested Frames** are frames contained within other frames, creating a hierarchy.

**Switching to Nested Frames:**

You must switch through the hierarchy sequentially:

```java
// HTML Structure:
// Main Page
//   └── Outer Frame
//         └── Inner Frame

// Start from main page
driver.switchTo().frame("outerFrame");  // Switch to outer frame
driver.switchTo().frame("innerFrame");  // Switch to inner frame

// Now in inner frame - can interact with its elements
WebElement button = driver.findElement(By.id("innerButton"));
button.click();
```

**Navigation Methods:**

**defaultContent()** - Returns to main page
```java
driver.switchTo().frame("outerFrame");
driver.switchTo().frame("innerFrame");
// Now in inner frame

driver.switchTo().defaultContent();
// Now back at main page (skipped outer frame)
```

**parentFrame()** - Returns to immediate parent frame
```java
driver.switchTo().frame("outerFrame");
driver.switchTo().frame("innerFrame");
// Now in inner frame

driver.switchTo().parentFrame();
// Now in outer frame (went up one level)

driver.switchTo().parentFrame();
// Now in main page
```

**Complete Example:**
```java
public class NestedFrameExample {
    public void handleNestedFrames(WebDriver driver) {
        System.out.println("=== Main Page ===");
        System.out.println("Title: " + driver.getTitle());

        // Switch to outer frame
        driver.switchTo().frame("outerFrame");
        System.out.println("=== Outer Frame ===");
        WebElement outerElement = driver.findElement(By.id("outerElement"));
        System.out.println("Outer text: " + outerElement.getText());

        // Switch to inner frame (nested inside outer)
        driver.switchTo().frame("innerFrame");
        System.out.println("=== Inner Frame ===");
        WebElement innerElement = driver.findElement(By.id("innerElement"));
        innerElement.click();

        // Option 1: Go to parent frame (outer frame)
        driver.switchTo().parentFrame();
        System.out.println("=== Back to Outer Frame ===");

        // Option 2: Go directly to main page
        driver.switchTo().defaultContent();
        System.out.println("=== Back to Main Page ===");
    }
}
```

**Navigation Diagram:**
```
Main Page
   |
   └── defaultContent() from anywhere goes here
   |
   └── Outer Frame
          |
          └── parentFrame() from inner goes here
          |
          └── Inner Frame
                 |
                 └── You are here
```

**Key Differences:**

| Method | Behavior | Use Case |
|--------|----------|----------|
| defaultContent() | Jump to main page | Reset to top level |
| parentFrame() | Go up one level | Navigate frame hierarchy |

**Best Practice:**
```java
public void switchToNestedFrame(String... framePath) {
    driver.switchTo().defaultContent();
    for (String frame : framePath) {
        driver.switchTo().frame(frame);
    }
}

// Usage
switchToNestedFrame("outerFrame", "innerFrame");
```

**Important:** You cannot jump directly to a nested frame. You must switch through each level of the hierarchy.

